Use the `clap` crate for simple, reliable command-line parsing.

**`Cargo.toml`**
```toml
[dependencies]
clap = { version = "4", features = ["derive"] }
```

**`src/main.rs`**
```rust
use clap::Parser;

#[derive(Parser, Debug)]
#[command(version, about)]
struct Args {
    /// Print extra information
    #[arg(short, long)]
    verbose: bool,

    /// Name to greet
    #[arg(short, long, default_value = "world")]
    name: String,
}

fn main() {
    let args = Args::parse();

    if args.verbose {
        println!("Verbose mode enabled");
    }

    println!("Hello, {}!", args.name);
}
```

Example usage:

```text
cargo run -- --name Alice --verbose
```

Output:

```text
Verbose mode enabled
Hello, Alice!
```

`clap` also automatically provides `--help` and `--version`.
